# Normalise everything to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# This is not cosmetic. Git on Windows defaults to converting text files to CRLF on checkout,
# and `deploy/*.sh` are piped straight into bash on a Linux host:
#
#     ssh ADMIN@MACHINE 'sudo bash -s' < deploy/server-setup.sh
#
# A CRLF checkout makes that fail with errors like `$'\r': command not found`, or worse,
# silently mangles a quoted string. Pinning eol=lf keeps the scripts runnable no matter which
# machine cloned the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.xlsx binary
*.db binary

# Jupyter notebooks are JSON with embedded base64 output images. Treating them as binary keeps
# a one-line change from producing a 100 KB diff.
*.ipynb -diff
